{
  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC -- see sections.json. This is ONE section's",
    "/v1/users/<uid>/grades?section_id=<id> payload. Deliberately awkward:",
    "  * an ungraded assignment (grade: null) must NOT render as 0",
    "  * a null comment alongside a real one",
    "  * `timestamp` is when the score was entered; it must stay OUT of `fp`,",
    "    because a teacher fixing a typo refreshes it and that would alert daily",
    "  * TWO gradebook entries sharing period id 'p2000001'. Real payloads",
    "    usually carry one, but a course placed in both terms carries two, and",
    "    period ids repeat across them -- so the period row id must be qualified",
    "    by the entry's own section_id or the two rows collapse onto one uid and",
    "    snapshot() silently drops one from every future diff.",
    "  * the entries' section_id values (1000000001 / 1000000009) deliberately",
    "    do NOT both match the roster id: attribution comes from the id that was",
    "    ASKED for, never from what the payload reports."
  ],
